# merge-policy - when the fleet's merge gate lets a passed PR merge without a re-test.
#
# Can, 2026-11-20 (request 521406): conflict-free PRs merge without a test run. Tests only for
# big conflicts or mission-critical work: board, vault, gateway, payments, store.
#
# The gate (gamebyte-ai/fleet lib/review_gate.py, policy_untested) reads this file from the base
# branch's head. With `mode clean-untested`, a reviewed PR with green CI on an older base merges
# with no re-test when it does not conflict with the base, changes no path below, and the base
# branch's own CI is green. Main's CI after each merge is the backstop.
#
# One rule per line: `<kind> <value>`.
#   mode      clean-untested turns the policy on. Delete that line to go back to the strict rule.
#   critical  a path prefix (plain string start; end it in / for a folder). A PR that changes a
#             file under one keeps the re-test on the current base.
# The fleet keeps a copy in gamebyte-ai/fleet config/merge-policies/<repo> (i_83ot570q).

mode clean-untested

# CI: how every test runs
critical .github/
critical scripts/build-skills-lock.mjs
# payments
critical skills/game-code/SKILL.md
critical skills/credit/
critical commands/account.md
# store
critical skills/store-prep/
critical commands/publish.md
# store privacy answers: what a game declares to the App Store and Google Play
critical skills/analytics/store-labels.md
critical skills/analytics/privacy.html
# what every user installs
critical install.sh
critical install.ps1
critical docs/install.sh
critical docs/install.ps1
critical bin/
critical .claude-plugin/
